OL,3,GNEWSAHow can Guernsey prepare for a
OL,4,Ahotter future?
OL,5,
OL,6,FGuernsey recently had its hottest
OL,7,Fsummer on record, with temperatures
OL,8,Fpeaking at 36.4B0C (97.52F) on 25 June.
OL,10,FIn August, the Jersey Met Office said
OL,11,Fthis was in line with evidence that
OL,12,Fclimate change was driving hotter
OL,13,Fsummers and increasing the likelihood
OL,14,Fof drier conditions.
OL,16,FProfessionals and businesses have
OL,17,Fhighlighted the actions they believe
OL,18,Fare needed from Guernsey in response to
OL,19,Fclimate change.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
